{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8ujeaGSubXepszsuSZF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the schema in `supabase/migrations/20260101000000_notes.sql`. I haven't run it against a database, so it is untested.\n\n- **Table:** `public.note` has `id` (uuid primary key, generated with `gen_random_uuid()`), `owner` (uuid, not null, references `auth.users`) and `body` (text, not null).\n- **Owner default:** `owner` defaults to `auth.uid()`, so a client doesn't have to send it. Deleting a user also deletes their notes.\n- **Row-level security:** it is enabled and forced on the table.\n  - Select, update and delete only work on rows where `owner` equals the signed-in user.\n  - Insert only accepts rows whose `owner` is the signed-in user, so nobody can create a note under someone else's name.\n  - Update also checks the new row, so a note can't be handed to another owner.\n- **Grants:** the `anon` role gets no access. The `authenticated` role gets select, insert, update and delete, and RLS limits those to the person's own rows.\n\nI also added an index on `owner`. I didn't build a user interface, as you asked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":32443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":636},"output_tokens":365,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19033adc-076c-4e59-954a-4b94351ed469","uuid":"22e4b0a8-6801-4f1f-828b-07ef70006dd0","timestamp":"2026-11-17T17:40:06.405Z","request_id":"req_011Ch8ujeDwDeSHBabkoKFZK"}
